        "Conditions evaluate to True or False. Comparison uses ==, assignment uses =. Confusing them is one of the most common beginner errors and produces a syntax error in Python, which is a kindness.",
        "Loops repeat. A for loop runs once per item in a collection; a while loop runs until a condition stops holding. An off-by-one error or a condition that never becomes false is the classic failure mode; tracing by hand is how you catch it." ] },
