      { t: "mc", c: "Rules vs learning", q: "What fundamentally changes when you move from rule-based software to machine learning?", opts: ["Programs run faster", "Humans supply examples and the system derives the mapping, instead of humans writing the rules", "The need for data disappears", "Correctness becomes guaranteed"], a: 1, e: "The rules are learned from data rather than specified. Correctness becomes statistical, not guaranteed." },
      { t: "sc", c: "AI suitability", q: "Which task is the poorest candidate for an LLM?", opts: ["Drafting quiz question variants", "Summarising learner feedback", "Computing final grades from weighted scores", "Suggesting tags for course content"], a: 2, e: "The grading rule is known and must be exact. Deterministic logic belongs in code; the model can explain the result afterwards." },
