        "Overfitting is memorising the training data instead of learning the pattern — excellent training scores, poor performance on anything new. It is the single most common failure in applied ML, and holding out data is how you detect it.",
        "Accuracy is misleading on imbalanced data. If 95% of learners pass a course, a model predicting 'pass' always is 95% accurate and completely useless. Precision, recall and the confusion matrix exist because a single number hides which errors you are making, and different errors have different costs." ] },
